-- title:
--   The measure |det g|⁻² dg is a bi-invariant Haar measure on GL₂(ℝ)
-- statement:
--   Equip $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$ with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra, generated by the topology of the group. Consider the measure [`RSCarrier.archMeasure`](def/LanglandsTunnell_RSCarrierSplit.html#L11) defined as follows: pull back Lebesgue measure on the space $\mathbb{R}^{2\times 2}$ of $2\times 2$ real matrices (viewed as functions $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathbb{R}$, with its volume measure) along the map sending an invertible matrix $g$ to its matrix of entries, and multiply the resulting measure by the density $g \mapsto (|\det g|^{2})^{-1}$, the inverse being taken in $[0,\infty]$ after applying $\mathrm{ENNReal.ofReal}$. The theorem asserts, with no hypotheses, the conjunction of two properties of this measure: it is a Haar measure, i.e. it is left invariant under the group law, finite on compact sets, positive on non-empty open sets and regular in the sense of Mathlib's `IsHaarMeasure`; and it is in addition invariant under right translations. Thus $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$ is unimodular and this explicit measure is a two-sided Haar measure on it.
--
--   This is the standard explicit description of Haar measure on $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$: Lebesgue measure on the four entries divided by $|\det|^{2}$, together with the unimodularity of $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$. It underlies the normalisation of the archimedean factor in the adelic Haar measure on $GL_2$ used for Rankin–Selberg integrals, and is cited when the global Haar measure is factored into local ones and when archimedean integrals are estimated via the Iwasawa decomposition.
